{"repo": {"name": {"en-US": "KabelWacht"}, "description": {"en-US": "Personal F-Droid repository that publishes signed KabelWacht releases, built automatically from tagged commits in CI."}, "icon": {"en-US": {"name": "/icons/icon.png", "sha256": "90b1acbe0c6b56ba5f9221a6310e2f2c028379aeade52b172f22b470d9dbc2a3", "size": 861}}, "address": "https://muelli.github.io/KabelWacht/fdroid/repo", "timestamp": 1785516117000, "categories": {"fdroid": {"name": {"en-US": "fdroid"}}}}, "packages": {"com.github.muelli.kabelwacht": {"metadata": {"added": 1785498229000, "categories": ["fdroid"], "lastUpdated": 1785516117000, "name": {"en-US": "KabelWacht"}, "summary": {"en-US": "A simple, free WireGuard VPN client: scan, import, and manage tunnels."}, "description": {"en-US": "KabelWacht is a minimal, fully free-software WireGuard® client for Android.\n\nIt does one thing well: manage WireGuard tunnels and connect.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Create, list, edit and delete WireGuard profiles.\n* Import a configuration by scanning a QR code.\n* Import a configuration from a .conf file.\n* One-tap connect/disconnect with a per-tunnel switch.\n* Userspace WireGuard backend — no root required.\n\nPrivacy and freedom:\n\n* 100% free and open-source software (AGPL-3.0-or-later).\n* No trackers, no analytics, no advertising.\n* No Google Play Services or other proprietary dependencies.\n* The only network connection made is your own WireGuard tunnel.\n\nBuilt on the official WireGuard tunnel library and the ZXing QR decoder.\n\nWireGuard is a registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld. This project is not\nofficially affiliated with or endorsed by the WireGuard project.\n"}, "icon": {"en-US": {"name": "/com.github.muelli.kabelwacht/en-US/icon_zzyLzh1Ecmt4ffPiOm_OK1Os0jQ8X5GkJIP8LQnJOh8=.png", "sha256": "cf3c8bce1d44726b787df3e23a6fce2b53acd2343c5f91a42483fc2d09c93a1f", "size": 6747}}, "preferredSigner": "040b7e628f09bc36f8dc026dfda6018b386f1df1a49302b79b948e46d556bd77"}, "versions": {"1c391cc6545b204